# Build-time configuration for production builds of the front end.
#
# This has to be a file rather than a Worker variable. `next build` inlines every
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into the client bundle as it compiles, and a Cloudflare
# `vars` entry does not exist yet at that point — it is bound to the Worker at
# runtime, long after the bundle is fixed. Setting it there produced a build that
# silently fell back to the localhost default and shipped it to production.
#
# Committing it is safe and deliberate: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is compiled into JavaScript
# that every visitor downloads, so this value is public by construction. Never
# put a secret in this file — it would be published the moment anyone loads the
# page. Secrets belong in the API's environment, which the browser never sees.
#
# Changing this requires a rebuild, not just a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://blender-battle-api.onrender.com/api/v1
